{
 "name": "table-size",
 "what": "the size of one small program for 32-bit ARM, in bytes: .text, .rodata and their sum, at four states of the headers and in four forms",
 "purpose_in_the_task_list": "Owner, 2026-11-14: a table costs only what is needed; another solution than the media type as a compile-time parameter or a table in the Template is looked for. This run measures the class form of the scalar writers (arms 4 and 5 of the probe scalar-writers, run scalar-writers-20261114T090839Z.json) against the word tables of f331cd1 and the state before the tables",
 "method": "one build of each state and form, no repetition; the size of each section is read with arm-linux-gnueabihf-size -A from the linked program; a size has no noise, so no round, median or spread is given; the size of each escape table that the linked program holds is read with arm-linux-gnueabihf-nm -S (nm of the host binutils reads the same files)",
 "states": {"4dac08e": "before the tables (before commit 5 of plan A4)", "f331cd1": "the five tables of 256 words of 8 bytes (the head of claude/escape-room-a before this run)", "f331cd1+class-tables": "f331cd1 with bench/probes/table-size/class-tables.patch applied to the exported escape.hpp: the class form of arm 4 of the probe scalar-writers, a table of 256 classes of one byte and a table of the words of the classes for each context", "f331cd1+class-fields": "f331cd1 with bench/probes/table-size/class-fields.patch: the class form of arm 5, the classes of the five contexts in bit fields of one table of 256 entries of 16 bits"},
 "forms": {"none": "compile(source) with no media type", "html": "compile(source, \"text/html\")", "json": "compile(source, \"application/json\")", "runtime": "compile(source, media type read through a volatile pointer, \"application/json\")"},
 "program": "bench/probes/table-size/probe.cpp: compiles one template of three tags, renders it over a std::map<std::string, std::string> and writes the answer with std::puts",
 "builds": "arm-linux-gnueabihf-g++-16 -std=c++23 -Os -mthumb -ffunction-sections -fdata-sections -Wall -Wextra -Werror, linked with -Wl,--gc-sections against the shared libstdc++, libgcc_s and libc; target armv7-a+fp, hard float (the defaults of the compiler)",
 "headers": "include/ of each state, exported with git archive; for a state <commit>+<name>, run.sh applies <name>.patch of the probe directory with patch -p1. In the exported copy of 4dac08e the script gives the lambda indent_at of compile.hpp the return type size_t, as d08686b has it. The patched headers passed the test programs output, media_type, escape, room and troff of f331cd1 with clang++-23 -std=c++23 and g++-16 -std=c++26 -freflection, -O2 -march=x86-64-v3 -Wall -Wextra -Werror, before this run; include/ of the repository is not changed",
